braessentials.pdf]]"],[16834,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[16846,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[16900,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[17266,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[17602,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[18652,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[18943,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[19387,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[19507,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[19510,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[19960,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[19963,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[19966,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[19972,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[19978,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[20191,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[20197,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[20200,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]"],[5987,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]\n\n[[commutativealgebra.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf]]"],[5978,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf]]"],[5945,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf]]\n\n[[foundationsofmath.pdf]]"],[3779,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]\n\n[[foundationsofmath.pdf]]"],[4910,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]\n\n[[foundationsofmath.pdf]]"],[4922,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]\n\n[[foundationsofmath.pdf]]"],[5228,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]\n\n[[foundationsofmath.pdf]]"],[5963,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]\n\n[[foundationsofmath.pdf]]"],[9694,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]\n\n[[foundationsofmath.pdf]]"],[13060,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]\n\n[[foundationsofmath.pdf]]"],[16177,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]\n\n[[foundationsofmath.pdf]]"],[20314,"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]\n\n[[foundationsofmath.pdf]]"],[21263,"[[Algebraic Expressions]] treats an expression as a structured combination of numbers, variables, operations, and grouping symbols. Its terms are separated by addition or subtraction, and numerical coefficients scale their variable parts. Like terms have identical variable factors and exponents, so the distributive property permits their coefficients to be combined. Unlike terms cannot be merged merely because they occur in the same expression.\n\nEvaluation substitutes specified values for variables and then follows the grouping and operation structure. Simplification produces an equivalent form by suppressing parentheses correctly, distributing factors, and combining like terms. Translation works in the other direction: verbal relationships such as a sum, difference, product, quotient, square, or reciprocal become symbolic expressions. The important discipline is preserving order and grouping rather than translating one word at a time without regard to the relationship described."],[21863,"[[Algorithmic Fairness and Justice]] addresses the way automated decisions can reproduce or intensify unequal treatment. Bias can enter through unrepresentative training data, labels, proxy variables, model objectives, deployment choices, historical discrimination, or automation bias among users. Predictive policing illustrates a feedback loop: concentrating enforcement in one area produces more recorded incidents there, which then appears to justify still more enforcement. Removing a protected attribute does not guarantee fairness because other variables can encode much the same social pattern.\n\nFairness is not a single technical metric. Different definitions can conflict, and disagreement often reflects competing theories of justice. Treating everyone identically may preserve an unequal starting point, while corrective measures such as affirmative action intentionally use group membership to address prior disadvantage. Ethical work must therefore connect quantitative tests to political judgment, affected communities, and the distribution of benefits and burdens. Diverse teams and bias-mitigation techniques help, but they cannot make a contested social decision value-free."],[330,"[[algorithms.epub]]"],[333,"[[algorithms.epub]]"],[399,"[[algorithms.epub]]"],[411,"[[algorithms.epub]]"],[669,"[[algorithms.epub]]"],[684,"[[algorithms.epub]]"],[696,"[[algorithms.epub]]"],[747,"[[algorithms.epub]]"],[1047,"[[algorithms.epub]]"],[1365,"[[al